{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38345318",
      "title": "Revisiting Objects & Classes",
      "sourceHash": "8e63f641da6b5ee7b4fa38d4e63ebb160c74cb44047091c1d74c0ceaf30cfda0",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.17,
          "en": "So now that we learned about functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.17,
          "end": 7.17,
          "en": "I want to come back to values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.17,
          "end": 11.13,
          "en": "And specifically, I want to come back to objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.13,
          "end": 13.38,
          "en": "As you should already know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.38,
          "end": 14.73,
          "en": "objects in JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.73,
          "end": 18.69,
          "en": "can be used to group multiple values together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.69,
          "end": 23.69,
          "en": "So for example, if I have a user name, which could be Max,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.57,
          "end": 27.03,
          "en": "which typically of course would not be hard coded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.03,
          "end": 29.16,
          "en": "but might be fetched from a server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.16,
          "end": 32.313,
          "en": "or from some HTML input on the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.15,
          "end": 37.5,
          "en": "and I have a user age, let's say, of 34.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.5,
          "end": 41.49,
          "en": "I could group these values together in an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.49,
          "end": 43.71,
          "en": "so that instead of defining them like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.71,
          "end": 45.96,
          "en": "I could have a user object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.96,
          "end": 47.43,
          "en": "which is created like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.43,
          "end": 49.74,
          "en": "by using opening and closing curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.74,
          "end": 52.92,
          "en": "on the right side of this equal sign here, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.92,
          "end": 56.25,
          "en": "And then there I could have a name property, as it's called,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.25,
          "end": 57.75,
          "en": "and a age property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.75,
          "end": 60.21,
          "en": "So I have key value pairs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.21,
          "end": 62.31,
          "en": "where the keys are up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.31,
          "end": 64.08,
          "en": "but should follow the naming rules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.08,
          "end": 65.55,
          "en": "you already learned about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.55,
          "end": 68.34,
          "en": "They also should, of course, be descriptive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.34,
          "end": 70.59,
          "en": "And then separated by a colon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.59,
          "end": 74.52,
          "en": "I have the value that should be stored under that key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.52,
          "end": 78,
          "en": "Now, this object could be used to output it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78,
          "end": 79.743,
          "en": "in the console, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 80.64,
          "end": 84.57,
          "en": "If I refresh this page here, I would see my user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.57,
          "end": 86.25,
          "en": "And in this JavaScript console,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.25,
          "end": 87.873,
          "en": "I can actually also explore it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.43,
          "end": 91.41,
          "en": "but I can also access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.41,
          "end": 94.5,
          "en": "individual fields of that user object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.5,
          "end": 95.67,
          "en": "or of any object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 95.67,
          "end": 97.59,
          "en": "by using the dot notation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 97.59,
          "end": 100.25999999999999,
          "en": "And then for example, I can just access and output,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 100.25999999999999,
          "end": 102.93,
          "en": "in this case, the name field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 102.93,
          "end": 105.99000000000001,
          "en": "So there, for now, if I reload this to get rid of the error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 105.99000000000001,
          "end": 107.42699999999999,
          "en": "I would see \"Max.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 108.27000000000001,
          "end": 111.15,
          "en": "And this dot here is the key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 111.15,
          "end": 113.55,
          "en": "to accessing values in an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 113.55,
          "end": 116.22,
          "en": "You use this dot notation to get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 116.22,
          "end": 118.38300000000001,
          "en": "to a value in an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 119.25,
          "end": 121.5,
          "en": "Now, besides key value pairs like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 121.5,
          "end": 124.23,
          "en": "objects can also store functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 124.23,
          "end": 127.32,
          "en": "which we then typically call methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 127.32,
          "end": 131.76,
          "en": "For example, here I could create a greet function like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 131.76,
          "end": 133.83,
          "en": "without the function keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 133.83,
          "end": 136.26,
          "en": "just the name of the function you want to have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 136.26,
          "end": 138.42000000000002,
          "en": "followed by the parentheses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 138.42000000000002,
          "end": 141.87,
          "en": "which could accept parameters if you wanted to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 141.87,
          "end": 143.82,
          "en": "And then your curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 143.82,
          "end": 145.77,
          "en": "And here you can return something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 145.77,
          "end": 149.343,
          "en": "or for example, simply console log something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 150.93,
          "end": 153.45,
          "en": "And then you could access this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 153.45,
          "end": 155.07,
          "en": "again with the dot notation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 155.07,
          "end": 157.07999999999998,
          "en": "and execute it like any other function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 157.07999999999998,
          "end": 158.853,
          "en": "by adding these parentheses here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 159.96,
          "end": 161.64,
          "en": "With that, if I reload this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 161.64,
          "end": 163.44299999999998,
          "en": "I would see \"Hello!\" here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 164.55,
          "end": 167.04,
          "en": "Now, if you are in such a method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 167.04,
          "end": 169.65,
          "en": "so in a function that belongs to an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 169.65,
          "end": 173.7,
          "en": "you can also access the properties of this object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 173.7,
          "end": 176.07,
          "en": "so the other methods and fields",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 176.07,
          "end": 177.57,
          "en": "that belong to this object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 177.57,
          "end": 179.733,
          "en": "with help of the special \"this\" keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 180.66,
          "end": 181.68,
          "en": "This would, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 181.68,
          "end": 183.63,
          "en": "allow me to output the age here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 183.63,
          "end": 188.433,
          "en": "by using this, which refers to this object, .age.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 189.57,
          "end": 191.88,
          "en": "And with that, if I reload this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 191.88,
          "end": 194.073,
          "en": "I would output the age here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 195.72,
          "end": 199.14,
          "en": "The this keyword won't be too important for this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 199.14,
          "end": 202.29,
          "en": "because we won't create too many methods here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 202.29,
          "end": 205.89,
          "en": "but nonetheless, it is a JavaScript concept you should know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 205.89,
          "end": 208.29,
          "en": "Now, when it comes to creating objects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 208.29,
          "end": 210.72,
          "en": "you can either create them like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 210.72,
          "end": 213.57,
          "en": "to group values together,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 213.57,
          "end": 216.18,
          "en": "or you can create blueprints",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 216.18,
          "end": 219,
          "en": "by using the special class keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 219,
          "end": 220.62,
          "en": "This is also an approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 220.62,
          "end": 222.72,
          "en": "we won't use too much in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 222.72,
          "end": 224.883,
          "en": "but I briefly want to mention it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 225.81,
          "end": 227.22,
          "en": "With the class keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 227.22,
          "end": 229.05,
          "en": "you can create a blueprint",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 229.05,
          "end": 233.67000000000002,
          "en": "that can then later be used to create the actual objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 233.67000000000002,
          "end": 238.53,
          "en": "Here we could create a blueprint called \"User,\" like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 238.53,
          "end": 241.62,
          "en": "And what's important here is that for class names,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 241.62,
          "end": 244.623,
          "en": "you should start with a capital case character.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 245.97,
          "end": 249,
          "en": "And then here you could, for example, add your methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 249,
          "end": 253.713,
          "en": "that should be part of that blueprint, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 255.18,
          "end": 258.18,
          "en": "In addition, you can add a so-called constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 258.18,
          "end": 261.15,
          "en": "by using the special constructor keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 261.15,
          "end": 262.08,
          "en": "which other than that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 262.08,
          "end": 264.72,
          "en": "is written like a normal function though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 264.72,
          "end": 268.56,
          "en": "and you can use this constructor for accepting parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 268.56,
          "end": 271.563,
          "en": "input values, like name and age, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 272.52,
          "end": 275.55,
          "en": "and then store them in properties of the object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 275.55,
          "end": 278.04,
          "en": "that will be created based on the class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 278.04,
          "end": 280.62,
          "en": "with help of the this keyword again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 280.62,
          "end": 282.78,
          "en": "So that's how I would create properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 282.78,
          "end": 284.97,
          "en": "named \"name\" and \"age\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 284.97,
          "end": 287.90999999999997,
          "en": "and store the parameter values \"name\" and \"age\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 287.90999999999997,
          "end": 289.503,
          "en": "in these properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 290.82,
          "end": 294.03,
          "en": "Now, by doing that alone, we won't achieve anything yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 294.03,
          "end": 297.39,
          "en": "Instead, we can now use such a class blueprint",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 297.39,
          "end": 300.84,
          "en": "by instantiating it with help of the special new keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 300.84,
          "end": 305.22,
          "en": "which creates a new object based on that blueprint.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 305.22,
          "end": 310.22,
          "en": "And then here I could pass \"Manuel\" and \"35\" as values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 311.58,
          "end": 314.82,
          "en": "And if I now console log user one here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 314.82,
          "end": 318.75,
          "en": "I would be getting an object, this object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 318.75,
          "end": 321.96,
          "en": "that is based on this blueprint.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 321.96,
          "end": 325.68,
          "en": "So this object here is based on this blueprint,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 325.68,
          "end": 328.8,
          "en": "and therefore it contains the values I passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 328.8,
          "end": 333.03,
          "en": "as input parameters to this constructor here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 333.03,
          "end": 335.58299999999997,
          "en": "That's how these things work together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 338.15999999999997,
          "end": 340.8,
          "en": "In addition, this user one object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 340.8,
          "end": 342.72,
          "en": "would now also have a greet method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 342.72,
          "end": 345.12,
          "en": "because I defined the greet method here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 345.12,
          "end": 347.943,
          "en": "So that's where this \"Hi!\" is coming from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 350.73,
          "end": 353.90999999999997,
          "en": "Again, we won't use this class keyword a lot in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 353.90999999999997,
          "end": 356.22,
          "en": "but you should know about it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 356.22,
          "end": 358.8,
          "en": "But with that, that's it for objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 358.8,
          "end": 361.683,
          "en": "I'm going to comment out of this code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 362.82,
          "end": 365.913,
          "en": "and we can continue with the refresher for the next concept.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}